Reason: tile_delete kept the id index current (patch 0063) by writing a new position for every tile after the deleted
one, ~4,800 hash writes when an early tile goes. A delete only moves the tiles after it one place down, and tile_add
only appends, so an entry at or past the lowest delete position is now left as it is, at most as many places too high
as there were deletes since; a lookup searches that short window downward and corrects the entry. After 64 deletes the
tail is rewritten once. Lookups give the same index as before.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

